<P>A <B>forklift</B> (also called a <B>lift truck</B>, a =
<B>high/low</B>, a=20
<B>stacker-truck</B>, or a <B>sideloader</B>) is a powered industrial <A =

title=3DTruck href=3D"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truck">truck</A> used =
to lift and=20
<A title=3DTransport =
href=3D"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transport">transport</A>=20
materials. The modern forklift was developed in the 1920s by various =
companies=20
including the <A title=3D"Transmission (mechanics)"=20
href=3D"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transmission_(mechanics)">transmissi=
on</A>=20
manufacturing company <A title=3D"Clark Material Handling Company"=20
href=3D"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clark_Material_Handling_Company">Cla=
rk</A>=20
and the hoist company <A title=3D"Yale Materials Handling Corporation"=20
href=3D"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yale_Materials_Handling_Corporation"=
>Yale=20
&amp; Towne Manufacturing</A>.<SUP class=3Dreference id=3Dcite_ref-0><A =
title=3D""=20
href=3D"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forklift#cite_note-0">[1]</A></SUP> =
The=20
forklift has since become an indispensable piece of equipment in =
manufacturing=20
and warehousing operations.</P>
